---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/apps/marsello';
const title = 'Marsello for Shopify: connect membership to the sale';
const desc = 'Evaluate Marsello POS identity, points earning, reward redemption, marketing permissions and retail operating costs.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">← All app reviews</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Shopify operations · checked November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Marsello for Shopify: connect membership to the sale</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Marsello is a candidate for retailers that want loyalty membership to work across Shopify online and in-store sales. Points, rewards and VIP tiers can give customers a reason to return and give staff a useful conversation at the register. The decision depends on reliable member identification and affordable reward economics, rather than a claimed supplier rank or an assumed repeat-purchase lift.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Start with the enabled stores and member identity</h2>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/marsello">current Shopify listing</a> describes loyalty with email and SMS marketing add-ons and supports Shopify POS. Treat loyalty and sending as separate scope decisions when getting a quote; do not assume every marketing feature is included in a loyalty subscription.</p>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-connect-my-shopify-site-to-marsello-marsello-help-center">Shopify sites guide</a> explains that online and POS sites are distinct and must be enabled separately. Confirm the online store and each intended retail site in the integration settings. A connected Shopify account is not evidence that every location is participating.</p>
      <p>Use a member who shops in both channels, a guest order, a corrected email and two people sharing a phone to inspect actual records. Establish which identifier staff use to attach the customer to a sale and who resolves duplicates. Do not merge identities solely because a shared household number matches. Membership, purchase history and separate email/SMS permissions must remain distinguishable.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Prove earning and redemption before promoting rewards</h2>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/shopify-pos-common-questions-marsello-help-center">POS common questions</a> describe the Scan, redeem loyalty rewards extension: add the customer to the sale, then open Show loyalty rewards to see the profile, points and available rewards. Points are deducted when a reward is applied. Install the extension on the intended registers and train staff using a controlled sale before announcing cross-channel redemption.</p>
      <p>Write acceptance cases for earning on a paid sale, a partial refund, a cancelled order, duplicate delivery of an order event and an attempted reward redemption with insufficient points. Reconcile the points ledger and sale discount, including an abandoned sale after a reward was applied. The <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-automatically-remove-loyalty-points-for-shopify-orders-marsello-help-center">points removal guide</a> is a starting point for configuring reversal rules, not proof that a merchant’s existing rules are correct.</p>
      <p>For online redemption, check the supported storefront experience and checkout prerequisites. The <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/shopify-ecommerce-common-questions-marsello-help-center">ecommerce FAQ</a> gives Shopify Plus and Shopify 2.0 theme requirements for the checkout Rewards block. It also says issued loyalty codes can still redeem after disconnection. A migration therefore needs a plan for outstanding codes and balances, rather than simply uninstalling the integration.</p>
      <p>Choose earn rates, reward costs, expiry rules, tier qualification and discount combinations before launch. Finance should model outstanding reward obligations and margin; staff should know what happens when a member has a reward but the basket is ineligible. A points balance is useful personalization context, not evidence that a points reminder converts better than a percentage offer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Four proposed retail workflow evaluations</h2>
      <p>These are illustrative exercises, not observed merchant results. Validate the required event, segment and message controls in the purchased account before implementing any sequence.</p>
      <p><strong>Boutique cross-sell:</strong> after an identified in-store dress purchase, propose an accessories email three days later. Confirm that the order and member match, the accessories are available online and promotional email is permitted. Recheck purchases and suppression at dispatch, cancel a stale incentive and assign one sender. Measure online contribution per eligible member with a randomized holdout, rather than claiming an 11% annual repeat-purchase gain.</p>
      <p><strong>Coffee equipment tier celebration:</strong> propose Gold at $500 qualifying spend and early access to a grinder launch. That threshold is a program design input, not a Marsello rule. Check how returns affect tier qualification and whether the customer has already bought the grinder. Email and SMS need separate permission and queue ownership. Compare eligible members with an eligible holdout, not a high-tier cohort with the general list.</p>
      <p><strong>Expiring points:</strong> propose 340 members with at least 50 points expiring in 14 days and no purchase in 90 days. Refresh balances immediately before selection and sending; a redemption must stop obsolete reminders. Explain the real expiry policy and reward conditions. Classify the message by its actual purpose and destination requirements, and report redemption and contribution after reward costs.</p>
      <p><strong>Referral membership:</strong> after a friend’s valid first order, propose an advocate reward and a welcome offer for the friend. Confirm identities, qualifying purchase, refund reversal and repeat-event handling. A referral does not grant permission to market to the friend. Track reward issuance once, distinguish existing customers from new members and measure incremental acquisition over a defined period; no 18% new-customer result or lower advertising CAC is established.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Budget the retail program rather than an invented merchant bill</h2>
      <p>Request a dated quote for one boutique POS site, the ecommerce site and 6,000 members; then quote a coffee retailer with two POS sites and referrals. Ask which customer count is billable, how locations are charged, which loyalty features are included and what email/SMS modules and message allowances add. Old $79–120 and $140–190 merchant bills are not verified current prices.</p>
      <p>Include POS subscriptions, staff training, integrations, creative work, reward discounts, returns and outstanding balances. As a hypothetical reward calculation, $100 of qualifying spend earning one point per dollar creates 100 points; a $5 reward costing 100 points has a face value of 5% of that spend. This is neither a supplier rate nor a complete margin calculation. Include redemption frequency and exclusions before adopting that design.</p>
      <p>For an online-only apparel store, compare the value of a maintained membership program against email/SMS needs alone. There is no demonstrated $89 wasted subscription or migration saving here. Order volume alone does not establish when loyalty becomes worthwhile; the ability to fund and operate the rewards matters.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mb-8">
      <h2>Choose the membership workflow and preserve continuity</h2>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="/apps/privy">Privy review</a> follows capture, offers and messaging continuity; Marsello’s distinctive acceptance case is a known member earning and redeeming at a register and online. The <a class="link" href="/apps/justuno">Justuno review</a> follows a storefront submission into a sender. Neither a popup signup nor a synced sender contact proves a working loyalty ledger.</p>
      <p>Keep Marsello on the shortlist where staff enrollment, cross-channel rewards and tier benefits justify the work. If evaluating a separate loyalty and messaging stack, require the same identity and reward reversal cases. Links to <a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a> or <a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy</a> are evaluation pointers, not a required supplier pairing or proof of superior segmentation.</p>
      <p>Assign ownership of enrollment copy, member corrections, reward exceptions, opt-outs and failed sends. Before promotional dispatch, recheck current channel permission, suppression and order state; membership is not SMS consent. Deduplicate event retries and cancel obsolete queues. During a change of tools, preserve permission evidence, balances and outstanding codes, and reconcile them before retiring the old process.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
